WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
So, I went from broke as hell, homeless

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.520
at one point, living in Section 8

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.720
housing and trailer parks, then getting

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.080
in an even worse situation because I

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.960
went $300,000 in student loan debt in

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.240
order to get a good degree and a good

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.600
job, all the way to making over $10

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.400
million online and being at the point

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.160
where I could literally retire anytime I

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.200
want in pretty much any place that I

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.360
want right now. And I did it all without

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.440
luck, talent, or a trust fund. And now

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.320
Claude AI and just AI in general makes

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.080
the whole thing faster than it's ever

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.320
been before. If I had a time machine, I

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.920
could go back to the younger version of

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.840
myself and tell them the things that I'm

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.680
going to tell you in this video, I would

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.640
have been able to do it significantly

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.920
faster. So, this video is going to be

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.440
what I wish I knew when I was 18 years

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.600
old. And with that being said, let's get

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.520
into rule number one. And that is get a

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.000
job first, right? So, this is the first

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.200
rule that basically no guru wants to say

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.120
out loud, right? Before you start a

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.240
business, get a job. And I know that

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.360
sounds backwards, so let me explain why

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.360
it's the smartest move that you can

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.840
make, right? Almost every business model

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.000
needs money to start and money to

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.360
survive while it grows. A job gives you

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.920
that runway and it removes the

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.519
desperation that kills most new

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.200
businesses. So, think of your job like

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:08.200
the runway and your business like the

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.960
plane. No plane takes off from a

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.400
standstill, right? It needs a runway to

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.800
take off, right? It needs the runway to

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.960
build up speed and then it lifts off on

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.680
its own. Your job is the runway that

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.640
gets your business moving. Now, not

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.880
every job is equal. There's some jobs

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.120
that are kind of just a dead end. So,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.920
let me talk about the ones that are

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.800
actually worth getting and why. So, the

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.480
first one is what I call a warm body

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.200
job. This is where you're paid mostly to

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.760
just be there. Think overnight shift at

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.520
a front desk, security, or a quiet IT

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.120
job. You do one or two hours of real

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.520
work and then you build your business

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.160
the rest of the time. And this job

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.840
actually does have a lot of value

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.440
because of the fact that you have so

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.080
much free time and of course you're

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.720
making enough to make a living and then

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.960
spend the money necessary to start a

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.680
business on the side. So, you're

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.360
essentially getting paid to learn

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.000
in-demand skills. So, the second type of

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.960
job is the same thing but in a different

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.880
way. So, it's a high-skilled job where

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:58.320
you're getting paid to learn something

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.840
valuable like sales or marketing, or

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.440
running ads, etc., etc. So, you get paid

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.400
while the skill itself makes you more

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.040
money. So, again, you're getting paid to

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.080
learn in-demand skills. So, the third is

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.360
what I call an intrapreneur job, right?

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.200
That is where you get so good and so

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.280
valuable at something that your company

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.720
pays you almost like a partner to keep

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.280
it. So, you're getting paid pretty close

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.800
to what an actual entrepreneur would

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.840
make without having to take on all the

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.600
risks of an entrepreneur. And this is

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.360
also really good because it's almost

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.200
like entrepreneurship with training

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.120
wheels. You are going to be working very

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.360
hard in a job like this. So, yeah, with

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.400
this type of job, you're not going to

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.240
have that much free time. It is quite

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.080
busy. But, you're going to be learning

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:37.120
invaluable skills. You're basically just

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.640
running a business. So, again, it's like

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.560
business with training wheels. And those

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.320
skills that you learn will be invaluable

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.920
for your future, whether you end up just

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.440
staying as an employee, or whether you

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.720
start your own business. Now, I love

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.240
this myself, right? I worked at a very

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.880
calm pharmacy job where I could

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:53.200
basically just get my work done in about

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.320
3 hours. And this was before COVID, of

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.080
